    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The `identityKey` field is generated on `OwnerDto`, MapStruct wires `ownerDto.setIdentityKey(owner.getIdentityKey())`, and it's serialized via `@JsonProperty(\"identityKey\")`. The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI consolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey` and made `POST /api/owners` reject with **409** only on a whole-key match.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`**\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a derived `getIdentityKey()` (mirroring the existing `getMembershipLevel`/`getContactPreference` derived getters), null-safe on each component.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, replaced `rejectDuplicateTelephone(...)` and `rejectDuplicateEmail(...)` with a single `rejectDuplicateIdentity(owner)` call, placed after telephone, household, and email are all resolved so the full key is available. `applyHousehold` no longer throws `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` \u2014 it now only assigns the shared `householdId` (which feeds the key); the rejection flows through the identity key instead. Removed the now-unused duplicate-check methods and imports.\n\n3. **`DuplicateOwnerIdentityException.java`** (new) + handler in **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 returns 409 with `errors: [\"identityKey\"]`.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` property to the Owner schema, so it's generated onto `OwnerDto`, auto-mapped by MapStruct, and **returned** on reads/creates.\n\nBehavioral consequence (as specified): because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones now have different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\nVerification: `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` passes (same telephone \u2192 same key \u2192 409), and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.",
